7. Register the jump animation in js/data/characters.js

#0001 currently defines only idle and run under animations.

Add a real jump animation using the newly added files.

Use the existing frames(BASE_0001, name, count) helper when the filenames follow the normal sequential convention.

The configuration should conceptually look like:

jump: {
  frames: frames(BASE_0001, 'jump', N),
  fps: 10,
  loop: false,
  heightRatio: 1,
},

where N is the real supplied frame count.

10 fps is a sensible starting playback speed for the non-looping jump sequence. If visual inspection of the supplied sequence clearly requires a slightly different rate, make the smallest reasonable adjustment and document it.

The jump animation must not loop continuously in mid-air.

The existing SpriteAnimator already leaves a non-looping animation on its final frame after playback reaches the end.

Do not add special-case #0001 animation code to the engine.

