9. Make falling continue to use the new airborne artwork

There are no dedicated falling sprites in the current repository.

Do not invent any.

When the character passes the apex, the state changes from jump to fall.

Instead of reverting to idle during descent, update the fall fallback so it resolves to the new jump animation and holds an appropriate airborne frame.

Unless inspection of the actual supplied frames clearly suggests another frame, use the final jump frame for falling.

For example, conceptually:

fall: {
  animation: 'jump',
  frame: N - 1,
},

The frame index is zero-based.

This gives the desired behavior:

* jump begins → jump sequence plays once
* if the sequence completes before the apex → final jump frame is held
* descent begins → final jump frame continues to be held
* landing → state returns normally to idle/run

Do not create a fake looping fall animation.

If the supplied sprite package actually contains separately identifiable fall/descent frames, use the real supplied art appropriately instead of forcing this fallback, but do not invent a separate fall animation without actual frames.

